(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ACCESS_CONTROL','Access control: Access to the dashboard is limited to authorized personnel only and data access can be limited based on role-based permissions.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ANALYZE_PERFORMANCE','Analyze the campaign performance data by drilling down from province to district to administrative post to locality to village level using the available charts.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ANS_DASHBOARD_USECASE_A','A dashboard is a visual representation of performance metrics and data related to a healthcare campaign. It provides an easy-to-understand overview of the campaign''s performance and monitoring the campaign. The data presented on the dashboard is aggregated and anonymized, ensuring the confidentiality of individual households and population data.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ANS_DASHBOARD_USECASE_B','The dashboard also enables analysis of the campaign''s performance at various levels and provides visualizations such as graphs and heat maps. Using a dashboard can help health campaign platform users make informed decisions, improve the campaign''s effectiveness, and ensure efficient delivery of healthcare services and interventions to the target population.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ANS_DATA_SECURITY','To ensure the security of data in the dashboard, several measures are implemented, including:',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ANS_GET_ALTERNATIVE','Alternatively, the country may have developed its own digital means of providing information to the dashboard or may use a platform similar to DIGIT. In any case, having a digital platform for managing and monitoring the healthcare campaign is essential for tracking progress and ensuring that the campaign''s objectives are met.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ANS_GET_CAMPAIGN','In the healthcare campaign, Field Level Workers (FLWs) are responsible for collecting and inputting data related to households and citizens. This data is crucial in analyzing the performance of the campaign, identifying areas that require attention and monitoring progress.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ANS_GET_CAMPAIGN_FLW','The FLWs share this data while providing campaign services and interventions, enabling the system to collect relevant data at the ground level. The data collected by the FLWs is then used to create a comprehensive overview of the campaign''s performance, which is presented on the campaign dashboard.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ANS_GET_HCM','The healthcare campaign management service in the country is based on DIGIT, a platform that provides tools to manage healthcare campaigns effectively. This platform streamlines the process of data collection, storage, and analysis, making it easier for FLWs and boundary-level users to input data into the system. The platform also provides tools to generate reports and visualizations, making it easier to monitor the campaign''s performance and identify areas for improvement.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ANS_GET_MANAGERS','Supervisors and warehouse managers, who are boundary-level users, also play a crucial role in providing datasets required for the dashboard. They contribute to the dashboard by providing data on the supply chain, stock management, and other relevant information. The datasets provided by these users are combined with the data collected by the FLWs to create a comprehensive picture of the healthcare campaign''s performance.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ANS_WHAT_CAN_DASHBOARD_VIEWER_SEE_AND_DO','The dashboard enables the user to view:',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_AREA_BOUNDARY','Performance metrics presented based on area boundaries.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_BOUNDARIES_DATA','Boundaries Data - This refers to the information gathered by field-level workers responsible for the assigned area of the campaign. This data is used to track progress and inform decision-making through the dashboard.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_CLARITY_ON_DASHBOARD','To clarify certain terms used in the dashboard:',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_COMPARE_PERFORMANCE','Compare the campaign performance of different districts within the province.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_DASHBOARD','About the Dashboard',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_DASHBOARD_DESIGN','The dashboard is designed to present a summary of the data collected through the front line app used for the delivery of health interventions. The data is aggregated, meaning it has been compiled and processed to create a comprehensive overview of the healthcare campaign''s performance. The information presented on the dashboard does not contain any personally identifiable details, such as Team worker names or any personal detail.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_DASHBOARD_OBJECTIVE','The primary objective of the dashboard is to provide an overview of the health campaign''s performance. The dashboard uses specific identifiers to categorize and organize the data, making it easier for viewers to understand and interpret the information presented.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_DASHBOARD_USE','With the Health Campaign Management Dashboard, users can quickly identify campaign progress, generate detailed summary reports with a single click, and measure the campaign coverage, and identify potential roadblocks. This information can help users to plan stock requirements and identify areas for planning future campaigns. Additionally, the dashboard enables users to track the progress rate of healthcare campaign services.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_DASHBOARD_USE_IDENTIFIERS','Using these identifiers, the dashboard can showcase the strengths and weaknesses of the healthcare campaign across various districts, administrative posts, localities or villages in the provinces, highlighting areas that require further attention and improvement.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_DATA_MASKING','Data masking: The sensitive data is masked to protect personally identifiable information, and only authorized personnel can access the unmasked data.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_ENCRYPTION','Encryption: The data transmitted to and from the dashboard is encrypted using secure communication protocols, such as HTTPS or SSL, to protect against interception and unauthorized access. The data can be encrypted to prevent unauthorized access and ensure data confidentiality. This can be done using secure encryption protocols such as AES or RSA.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_FOLLOWING_VIEWER_DO_ON_DASHBOARD','On the dashboard, the user can:',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_KEY_TERMS','Key Terms',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_MONITOR_PERFORMANCE','Monitor campaign performance at all boundary levels of the province.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_PERFORMANCES_IN_FORM_VISUALIZATIONS','Performance metrics are presented through visualizations such as graphs and heat maps.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_PERFORMANCE_METRICS','Performance metrics for the healthcare campaign.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_PURPOSE','Purpose',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_PURPOSE_DEFINE','The purpose of the dashboard is to ensure data transparency, provide easy access to data, promote accountability, and facilitate data-driven decision-making.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_PURPOSE_INFO','The Health Campaign Management DIGIT Dashboard is a Decision Support System (DSS) tool that provides health campaign management teams with a consolidated and interactive dashboard. The dashboard presents key metrics in a visually appealing format, making it easier for users to understand campaign progress, stock efficiency, and areas for improvement.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_QUES_DASHBOARD_USE','Why is a dashboard used in healthcare campaigns?',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_QUES_GET_DATA_FROM_DASHBOARD','Where does the data for the dashboard come from?',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_QUES_HOW_DATA_SECURED','How is this data secured?',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_QUES_WHAT_CAN_DASHBOARD_VIEWER_SEE_AND_DO','What can the user of the dashboard see and do?',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_QUES_WHAT_IS_DATA','What is ‘data’?',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_REGULAR_BACKUPS','Regular backups:  The data can be regularly backed up to prevent data loss in the event of a security breach or system failure.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_REGULAR_SECURITY_AUDITS','Regular security audits: Regular security audits should be conducted to ensure that the dashboard remains secure and to identify and fix any security vulnerabilities that may arise.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_SECURE_HOSTING','Secure hosting: The dashboard should be hosted on a secure server that is regularly updated with security patches and other security measures to prevent hacking and data breaches.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_SERVICE_LEVEL_PERFORMANCE','Performance metrics presented at various levels, including province, district, administrative post, locality and village.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_UNIQUE_CHAR','# / % - In the dashboard, the "#" symbol represents data that is displayed as a count, while the "%" symbol represents data that is displayed as a percentage. These symbols are used to identify the format in which the data is presented in the dashboard.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABOUT_USERS_DEFINE','Users - These are the.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ABSENT_WORKERS_ONCE','Absent Workers',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ATTENDED_WORKERS','Attended Workers',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_ATTENDED_WORKERS_PERCENT','% Attended Workers',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATIONS','Calculations',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_AVERAGE_COMPLAINTS_RESOLUTION_TIME_HOURS_BAR','Average Complaint Resolution Time (Hrs)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_AVERAGE_COMPLAINTS_RESOLUTION_TIME_HOURS_BAR_FIVE','The Boundary data could be ‘districts’ for provincial/national users and ‘Administrative posts’ for district user roles.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_AVERAGE_COMPLAINTS_RESOLUTION_TIME_HOURS_BAR_FOUR','The average complaint resolution time is then calculated by adding all resolved and rejected complaints time and then dividing it by the total number of resolved and rejected complaints for that particular boundary and date range. This calculation gives the average time taken to resolve a complaint for that boundary.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_AVERAGE_COMPLAINTS_RESOLUTION_TIME_HOURS_BAR_ONE','The Average Complaint Resolution and Response Time chart is used to show the average time taken to resolve a complaint for each boundary. The chart will be a bar chart, with the y-axis showing the average time taken in hours and the x-axis showing the different boundaries.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_AVERAGE_COMPLAINTS_RESOLUTION_TIME_HOURS_BAR_SIX','The bar chart will show the average complaint resolution time for each boundary, with the height of each bar representing the average time taken to resolve a complaint. This chart helps to identify which boundaries are taking longer to resolve complaints and could indicate areas where improvements are needed to improve the complaint resolution process.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_AVERAGE_COMPLAINTS_RESOLUTION_TIME_HOURS_BAR_THREE','For each ‘resolved’ complaint, we calculate the difference in time between the time at which the complaint was created and the time at which it was resolved. Similarly, for each ‘rejected’ complaint, we calculate the difference in time between the time at which the complaint was created and the time at which it was rejected. ',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_AVERAGE_COMPLAINTS_RESOLUTION_TIME_HOURS_BAR_TWO','To calculate the average complaint resolution time, only those complaints whose statuses are either ''REJECTED'' or ''RESOLVED'' (within the selected date range) should be considered.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_BOUNDARY_WISE_SHARE_OF_COMPLAINTS','Boundary Wise Share Of Complaints',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_BOUNDARY_WISE_SHARE_OF_COMPLAINTS_FOUR','To validate the accuracy of the chart, the sum total of all bars should be equal to 100%.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_BOUNDARY_WISE_SHARE_OF_COMPLAINTS_ONE','The "Boundary Wise Share of Complaints" is a bar chart that shows the percentage share of complaints created for each boundary within a selected date range. The chart is based on two data sources: Boundary Data from the MDMS and Complaints data from the Complaints module in the mobile application.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_BOUNDARY_WISE_SHARE_OF_COMPLAINTS_THREE','For National and Provincial Users, the boundaries are ‘districts’, whereas for District Users, the boundaries are ‘administrative posts’. The chart shows the distribution of total complaints across different boundaries, allowing the user to identify which boundaries have the highest and lowest number of complaints created within the selected date range.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_BOUNDARY_WISE_SHARE_OF_COMPLAINTS_TWO','Each bar of the chart represents a specific boundary, which can be a district or an administrative province (AP) as per the user role. Each bar of the chart represents the percentage share of complaints created for that boundary, out of the total complaints created in all the boundaries.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_BOUNDARY','Complaints By Boundary',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_BOUNDARY_FOUR','However, the complaints where status=Created should not be considered to avoid repetition.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_BOUNDARY_ONE','This bar chart presents the total number of complaints by boundary for the selected date range. The data source for this chart is the Complaints module in the mobile application, and the boundary data is obtained from the MDMS.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_BOUNDARY_THREE','Each bar in the graph represents the total number of complaints for a specific boundary. The total complaints for each boundary will be calculated as the sum of open, resolved, and rejected complaints, during the selected date range. The date range is selected from the date range filter on the dashboard.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_BOUNDARY_TWO','The chart is displayed as a bar chart with the number of complaints on the y-axis and the boundary data on the x-axis. The boundary data is districts for National & Provincial users and administrative posts for District users.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_STATUS','Complaints By Status',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_STATUS_FIVE','It is important to note that the complaints where status is ‘Created’ are not considered to avoid repetition.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_STATUS_FOUR','The x-axis of the chart represents the selected boundary (district or administrative post), and the y-axis represents the number of complaints. The total number of complaints is calculated as the sum of Open, Resolved, and Rejected complaints.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_STATUS_ONE','The "Complaints by Status" chart is a stacked bar chart that shows the distribution of complaints by their status (Open, Resolved, and Rejected) across different boundaries (districts or administrative posts) for a selected date range.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_STATUS_THREE','There are two toggle options for the chart - ‘number’ toggle and ‘percentage’ toggle. When the number toggle is selected, the chart displays the absolute count of complaints for each status. When the percentage toggle is selected, the chart shows the percentage distribution of complaints for each status.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_STATUS_TWO','The calculation involves counting the total number of complaints created for a selected boundary (province, district, or administrative post) for a date range. Then, for each boundary, the number of complaints that are Open, Resolved, and Rejected are counted and represented as a stack in the bar chart.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE','Complaints By Type',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE_FOUR','For national and provincial users, the selected province will be the boundary data, while for district users, the assigned district will be the boundary data.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE_ONE','The "Complaints by Type" have a pie chart that shows the total number of complaints by their types in a selected province or district for a date range. As this report is presented in a pie chart format, where each slice of the pie represents a specific complaint type.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE_STACKED_BAR','Complaints By Type',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE_STACKED_BAR_FIVE','The x-axis of the chart represents the different boundaries, with districts displayed for National and Provincial users and administrative posts displayed for District users. Each bar of the graph shows the total complaints stacked with the complaint type, boundary, and date range.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE_STACKED_BAR_FOUR','For the percentage toggle, each stack of the bar represents the percentage of complaints for a specific complaint type within a particular boundary and date range, calculated as a percentage of the total complaints for that boundary.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE_STACKED_BAR_ONE','The ‘Complaints by Type’ stacked bar chart shows the total number of complaints by their type for the selected date range, displayed as a stacked bar chart. The chart is divided into sections, with each section representing a different type of complaint, such as Logged, Synced, or Crashed etc…',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE_STACKED_BAR_SIX','To ensure accuracy, the sum total of all complaint types for a particular boundary should be equal to the total complaints for that boundary.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE_STACKED_BAR_THREE','The chart can be toggled between showing the ‘number’ of complaints and the ‘percentage’ of complaints for each complaint type. For the number toggle, each stack of the bar represents the total number of complaints for a specific complaint type within a particular boundary and date range.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE_STACKED_BAR_TWO','The data for the chart is taken from the Complaints module in the mobile application and is organized by boundary data from MDMS. The total number of complaints for each boundary is calculated by summing all complaints created for that boundary and within the selected date range.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE_THREE','The data of the "Complaints" module is taken from the mobile application, which is available in the MDMS. The complaint types will be predetermined values, such as "App Malfunction," "Login error," "Sync error," "Forgot password," and "Others," which are configured in the MDMS.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_BY_TYPE_TWO','The percentage of each slice is calculated based on the total number of complaints for that specific type and the total number of complaints for the selected boundary role user. The count of complaints for each type will also be displayed as a tooltip when hovering over the slice of the pie.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_COMPLAINTS_TAB_OVERVIEW_ONE','A section of the dashboard displaying analytics on complaints, including complaint type, response, and status. This information can be used to make improvements to the complaint handling process and to address any recurring issues.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INTVENTORY','Number Of Days To Last Inventory',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INTVENTORY_ONE','The ''Number of days to last inventory'' is a metric that represents the number of days the current inventory of bednets can last based on the current rate of consumption. This metric is useful for the dashboard users to determine when to order more bednets to ensure that there is an adequate supply to meet the demand.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INTVENTORY_POINTS_HEADING','The calculation involves the following steps:',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INTVENTORY_POINT_FOUR','Number of days the inventory can last based on the current consumption rate, this is calculated as the ‘total stock on hand’ divided by the total expected consumption for all warehouses within the boundary.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INTVENTORY_POINT_ONE','Determine the stock on hand as of today''s date for each warehouse in the district or administrative post.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INTVENTORY_POINT_THREE','Calculate the total expected consumption for all warehouses within the boundary. This is calculated as the sum of the bed nets of the stock on hand for each warehouse and the daily microplan target for the district or administrative post.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INTVENTORY_POINT_TWO','Calculate the daily microplan target for bed nets.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INTVENTORY_THREE','It is important to note that the micro plan target should be set based on the daily bednet target for the province and the stock on hand should be considered for all warehouses within the boundary of the district or administrative post.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INTVENTORY_TWO','To calculate this metric, the application uses the inventory management data from the ''Stock Reconciliation'' page, which includes the stock on hand for each warehouse individually. The calculation takes into account the daily microplan targets for bednets and the total number of warehouses within the boundary of the district or administrative post.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_STOCK_IN_HAND','Stock In Hand',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_STOCK_IN_HAND_ONE','The "Stock in Hand” metric represents the total available and Required bednets as of today in each boundary according to the last updated data. This metric is calculated using the Inventory Management data from the Stock reconciliation page of the application, which includes the stock on hand for the current day. The calculation for the side-by-side bar graph is done as:',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_STOCK_IN_HAND_POINT_ONE','Calculate the number of ‘available’ bednets (Blue Bar): Get the stock in hand for the current day from the Inventory Management data. This includes the stock in hand day plus any stock received, minus any stock issued, returned on the current day. Further calculate the total available bed nets in each warehouse for the given boundary (District or Administrative Posts) by multiplying the daily micro plan target by the number of campaign days and summing across all warehouses.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_STOCK_IN_HAND_POINT_TWO','Calculate the number of required bednets (Orange Bar): The bed nets required for the boundary as per the micro plan for the entire campaign duration based on the project setup. Further now calculate the cumulative bed nets distributed so far. Calculate the remaining bed nets required by subtracting the cumulative bed nets distributed from the bed nets required.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_STOCK_IN_HAND_TWO','The resulting metric is represented as a side-by-side bar chart that shows the number of ‘available’ bednets and the actual ‘required’ number of bednets for each boundary. The "Available" bars are represented in blue, and the "Required" bars are represented in orange. The metric is presented in a default view of district-wise for national and provincial users and administrative-post wise for district-level users.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT','Summary Report',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_BOUNDARY_NAME','Boundary Name',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_BOUNDARY_NAME_ONE','The boundary column in the summary report table indicates the level of division for which the stock report is being displayed. For National and Provincial level users, the boundary column will display the names of the districts, whereas for District level users, the boundary column will display the names of the administrative posts.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_BOUNDARY_NAME_TWO','This column is used to group and organize the stock data for each division. The drill-down feature can be used to view the stock detail for all warehouses within a specific boundary at the granular level.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_DAYS_TO_LAST','Days To Last',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_DAYS_TO_LAST_FOUR','In summary, the "Days to last" column provides valuable information on the number of days that the current stock of bednets can last, based on the current rate of distribution and consumption, which is calculated by dividing the total number of bednets in stock by the daily microplan target.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_DAYS_TO_LAST_ONE','The "Days to last" column in the summary report refers to the number of days that the bednets currently in stock can last, based on the current rate of distribution and consumption. This is calculated by dividing the total number of bednets currently in stock, denoted as ''c'', by the daily microplan target, denoted as ''b''.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_DAYS_TO_LAST_THREE','The total number of bednets in stock, denoted as ''c'', is the sum of bednets across all warehouses under this boundary. The value of ''b'' is the daily microplan target for the bednets, which is set in the project setup. Finally, the value of "Days to Last" , denoted, is calculated as c/b.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_DAYS_TO_LAST_TWO','To calculate the total number of bednets in stock, we need to use the stock reconciliation page, which calculates the stock on hand for the current day, denoted as ''a''. This is calculated by adding the stock in hand from the previous day with the stock received and returned, and then subtracting the stock issued.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_DISTRIBUTED','Nets Distributed',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_DISTRIBUTED_ONE','The "Nets distributed" column in the summary report shows the number of nets that were distributed during the selected date range. The calculation is based on the quantity of nets recorded in the "Record Stock issued" form in the Inventory Management system for each warehouse under the boundary. The sum of the quantity of nets distributed across all warehouses under the boundary is then displayed in the "Nets distributed" column.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_DISTRIBUTED_TWO','To calculate the "Nets distributed" column, the system first looks at the quantity of nets distributed from each warehouse during the selected date range. It then adds up these quantities across all warehouses under the boundary. Finally, the total quantity of nets distributed is displayed in the "Nets distributed" column of the summary report for the selected boundary.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_IN_STOCK','Nets In Stock',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_IN_STOCK_ONE','The "Nets in Stock" column in the summary report represents the total number of available bed nets in each boundary, according to the last updated data. This figure is calculated by summing up the number of nets across all warehouses under the boundary. The "Stock on Hand" column in the stock reconciliation page. The figure is then summed up across all warehouses under the boundary to obtain the total number of bed nets available in the boundary.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_IN_STOCK_TWO','The resulting figure is then entered into the "Nets in Stock" column in the summary report, which is further divided into warehouse details, micro plan targets for nets, and warehouse boundary details, depending on the project setup.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_RECEIVED','Nets Received',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_RECEIVED_ONE','In the summary report, "Nets received" refers to the total number of bed nets that were actually received for the selected date range in all the warehouses under the specific boundary. This metric is calculated by summing up the quantity received from each warehouse within the boundary.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_RECEIVED_TWO','The data for this metric is collected from the "Inventory Management" module, specifically from the "Record Stock received form" where the quantity received for each shipment is recorded. The warehouse name/ID and the boundary details are also recorded during project setup.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_RETURNED','Nets Returned',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_RETURNED_ONE','The "Nets returned" column in the summary report represents the total number of nets returned for the selected date range. This includes all the nets returned across all the warehouses within the selected boundary.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_RETURNED_THREE','The sum of the quantity of nets returned across all the warehouses within the selected boundary is calculated using this formula to give the final value for the "Nets returned" column in the summary report.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_RETURNED_TWO','The calculation for this column involves collecting the quantity of nets returned for the date range selection from each warehouse under the selected boundary, and then summing them up to get the total number of nets returned. This is done using the "Quantity returned" field in the Inventory Management module''s "Record Stock returned" form.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_TO_RECEIVE_AS_PER_MICROPLAN','Nets to receive as per microplan',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_TO_RECEIVE_AS_PER_MICROPLAN_FOUR','This point is important as it helps in determining whether the actual number of bed nets received is meeting the planned targets or not. It can also help in identifying any discrepancies or gaps in the warehouse management system.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_TO_RECEIVE_AS_PER_MICROPLAN_ONE','The "Nets to receive as per micro plan" point in the summary report refers to the number of bed nets that were planned to be received as per the micro plan for a specific boundary such as a district or administrative post. This value is calculated based on the micro plan targets for the bed nets that were set up during the project setup phase.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_TO_RECEIVE_AS_PER_MICROPLAN_THREE','This point is important as it helps in determining whether the actual number of bed nets received is meeting the planned targets or not. It can also help in identifying any discrepancies or gaps in the supply chain and logistics management system.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_NETS_TO_RECEIVE_AS_PER_MICROPLAN_TWO','The calculation takes into account the number of bed nets received across all warehouses under the boundary for a specific date range. It is calculated by summing up the quantity received for each warehouse and multiplying it with the total number of warehouses for that boundary.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_ONE','A summary report is a consolidated report that provides an overview of the inventory stock at the boundary level. The report includes all the warehouses within the boundary, and it is generated by aggregating data from individual warehouse reports.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_SUMMARY_REPORT_TWO','The summary report can be accessed by users at different levels. For national and provincial-level users, the report shows the stock details for each district, while for district-level users, the report shows the stock details for each administrative post (AP) within the district.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_TAB_OVERVIEW_ONE','The "Inventory" section is a part of the dashboard that provides data analytics related to inventory and warehouse management. This section is designed to give users an update on the stock levels and consumption trends. The data for this section is sourced from the warehouse manager application, which allows users to see data on inventory levels, stock movements, and consumption patterns.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_TAB_OVERVIEW_TWO',' By utilizing the information in the "Inventory" section, dashboard users can make informed decisions on inventory management, including reordering and restocking, to ensure that their warehouses are efficiently managed and inventory levels are maintained at optimal levels. Overall, the "Inventory" section provides valuable insights into warehouse management and inventory control.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_WAREHOUSE_DISTRIBUTION','Warehouse Distribution',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_WAREHOUSE_DISTRIBUTION_FOUR','The status of the warehouse is also indicated, with the ''Sufficient'' label indicating that the stock levels are expected to last until the end of the campaign, and the ''Insufficient'' label indicating that the stock levels are expected to run out before the end of the campaign.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_WAREHOUSE_DISTRIBUTION_ONE','This shows a geo map that is a visual representation of the locations of all the warehouses within the boundary, marked with their corresponding latitude and longitude coordinates. This map is integrated with the inventory management system and allows the user to click on any warehouse and view its details such as the warehouse ID, stock received, stock distributed, stock returned, stock in hand, and how long the stock will last based on the current consumption rate.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_WAREHOUSE_DISTRIBUTION_THREE','Clicking on a warehouse on the map will open up and display the detailed information about that particular warehouse. This information includes the warehouse ID, the stock received, stock distributed, stock returned, stock in hand, and how long the stock is expected to last based on the current consumption rate. ',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_INVENTORY_WAREHOUSE_DISTRIBUTION_TWO','The inventory data for each warehouse is captured in the backend of the mobile application and is displayed on the map as its detail. The map can be zoomed in and out to provide a better view of the location of the warehouses.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED','Bed Nets Distributed',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_TODAY','Bed Nets Distributed Today',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_TODAY_ONE','The KPI "Bed nets Distributed Today" represents the total number of bed nets distributed today across all provinces. This metric is calculated by adding up the number of bed nets distributed for each household across all provinces for the date range of today. The data source for this KPI is the Delivery Intervention Screen, which provides the number of bed nets distributed for each household.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_TODAY_TWO','This Insight is also available where the percentage change in bed nets distributed from the previous day to the current day is measured, which provides additional insights into the performance of the distribution campaign.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_COVERAGE_BY_PROVINCE','Coverage By Province',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLDS','Households',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_TODAY','Households Visited Today',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_TODAY_FIVE','This formula is used to calculate the percentage change in the number of households visited between "today" and the "previous day". The result of this calculation provides insight into the trend of households visited over time.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_TODAY_FOUR','((Today - Previous day) / Previous day) * 100',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_TODAY_ONE','The calculation for "Households Visited Today" KPI is as follows:',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_TODAY_THREE','The formula for calculating the percentage change between "Today" and "Previous day" is:',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_TODAY_TWO','First, the total number of households visited for current day i.e today is calculated for each province. Then, the aggregate of all households visited across all provinces for "today" is calculated.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLD_COVERAGE','Household Coverage (%)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLD_COVERAGE_FOUR','Additionally, hovering over the province or district the metric can also provide an insight into the change in coverage from the previous day, expressed as a percentage.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLD_COVERAGE_ONE','The Household Coverage (%) metric shows the percentage of households visited compared to the micro plan targets for each province and district. The micro plan targets are set up at the project setup phase.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLD_COVERAGE_THREE','For the zoom-in/drill-down view, the calculation is the same, but using district targets instead of province targets.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_HOUSEHOLD_COVERAGE_TWO','The calculation for the default view at the national level is, the total number of households visited until today divided by the household micro plan target for each province, multiplied by 100.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_POPULATION_COVERAGE','Population Coverage (%)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_POPULATION_COVERAGE_FIVE','Additionally hovering over the province or district the metric also includes an applicable insight, which is to measure the percentage change in population coverage from the previous day.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_POPULATION_COVERAGE_FOUR','For the zoom-in/drill-down view, the formula is the same, but for each district within the selected province.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_POPULATION_COVERAGE_ONE','The population coverage (%) achieved against micro plan targets shows a heat map of the coverage percentage across different provinces. The micro plan targets are set up during the project setup, and the population data is obtained from the delivery intervention screen, the calculation takes into account the campaign start date from the campaign setup date and boundary data from MDMS.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_POPULATION_COVERAGE_THREE','For the “default view” at the national level, the formula is the sum of the population covered (bed nets distributed) for each province divided by the population micro plan target for that province, all multiplied by 100.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_POPULATION_COVERAGE_TWO','Note: It is assumed that, the total number of bednets that have been delivered to the household, is the total number of population covered.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_POPULATION_COVERED','Population Covered',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_POPULATION_COVERED_TODAY','Population Covered Today',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_POPULATION_COVERED_TODAY_ONE','The "Population Covered Today" metric shows the total number of people covered by the campaign in all provinces for the current day. The population data used for the calculation is sourced from the “Registration and Delivery” FLWs application, and the bednets quantity distributed is taken into consideration.In addition to this, the "Additional Insights" show the percentage change in population coverage from the previous day to the current day.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED','Total Bed Nets Distributed (Cumulative)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_ONE','The Total Bed Nets distributed (Cumulative) is the total number of bednets distributed since the start of the campaign across all provinces. It shows the sum of bednets distributed for each province since the beginning of the campaign. Bed Nets distributed data can be obtained from the Delivery Intervention Screen as "a".',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_THREE','It can be written as Σx [ Σi(a)i ], for date range (Campaign start date - TODAY).',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_TWO','The Campaign Start Date is recorded as the Project Setup date. The calculation can be expressed as the sum of bednets distributed for each household (i) in each province (x) for the date range from the Campaign Start Date to Today.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_TOTAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED','Total Households Visited (Cumulative)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_TOTAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_ONE','The "Total Households Visited (Cumulative)" metric represents the total number of households that have been visited since the start of the campaign across all provinces.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_TOTAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_THREE','The calculation for this metric involves summing up the total number of households visited for each province from the campaign start date up to the current date.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_TOTAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_TWO','This metric takes into account all households visited in each province since the campaign start date, which is set up during campaign setup.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED','Total Population Covered (Cumulative)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_ONE','The Total Population Covered (Cumulative) is the sum of population covered for all provinces, since the start of the campaign. The data for population and quantity distributed is taken from the Delivery Intervention update Screen. The Campaign Start Date is the date when the campaign project was set up.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_NATIONAL_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_TWO','The calculation formula is the sum of households visited in each province multiplied by the average population per household, for the date range from the Campaign Start Date to Today. The result is the total population covered for all provinces since the start of the campaign.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_BEDNETS_COVERAGE_CUMULATIVE','Bed nets coverage (Cumulative)',1,now(),1,now()),
