(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_HOUSEHOLD_COVERAGE_RANKING_FOUR','The data required for the calculation will be obtained from the project setup and the application. The household coverage will be calculated based on the households visited which will be taken from the data submitted by the application. The household microplan target will be taken from the project setup.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_HOUSEHOLD_COVERAGE_RANKING_ONE','The Household Coverage Ranking is in percentage and provides a visual representation of the performance of different districts or administrative posts in terms of achieving household coverage targets. The chart will be displayed as a bar chart in descending order from left to right.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_HOUSEHOLD_COVERAGE_RANKING_THREE','For the national level role, the ranking will be provided for all the districts within the selected province. For the provincial level role, the ranking will be provided for all the districts within the respective province. For the district level role, the ranking will be provided for all the administrative posts within the respective district.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_HOUSEHOLD_COVERAGE_RANKING_TWO','The calculation will be based on the ratio of the total households visited till today to the household microplan target for each district or administrative post. The result will be expressed as a percentage.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INVENTORY','Number Of Days To Last Inventory',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INVENTORY_FIVE','It is important to note that when calculating the total number of bed nets needed per day, the micro plan target should be based on the daily bed nets target for the province for national and provincial level users, and the district for district level users. Additionally, the sum total of "stock in hand" across all warehouses should be considered when calculating the number of days the inventory can last.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INVENTORY_FOUR','The number of days the inventory can last is then obtained by dividing the total stock in hand by the total number of bed nets needed per day.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INVENTORY_ONE','The "Number Of Days To Last Inventory" is a bar chart that measures and displays how long the current inventory of bed nets can last based on the current rate of consumption. The metric is calculated by dividing the total number of bed nets in stock for all the warehouses for the boundary by the average daily consumption rate.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INVENTORY_SIX','Overall, this metric provides an indication of the adequacy of bed net stocks and the need for replenishment to ensure that there are enough bed nets to meet the demand for campaign fulfillment.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INVENTORY_THREE','The calculation for this metric involves obtaining the current "stock in hand" for each warehouse within the selected district, as obtained from the stock reconciliation page in the inventory management system. The daily bed nets microplan target is then obtained from the project setup data, and the total number of bed nets needed is calculated as the product of the daily target and the total number of warehouses in the district. ',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_NO_OF_DAYS_TO_LAST_INVENTORY_TWO','The bar chart will display the number of days the current inventory can last for each district within the selected province for national and provincial level users, and for each administrative post within the respective district for district level users.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_OVERALL_CHECKLISTS_COMPLETION_RATE','Overall Checklists Completion Rate',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_OVERALL_CHECKLISTS_COMPLETION_RATE_FIVE','The completion rate is then calculated as a percentage by dividing the Mandated Checklist completion rate by the Actual Checklist completion rate and multiplying the result by 100.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_OVERALL_CHECKLISTS_COMPLETION_RATE_FOUR','The ‘Actual National/Provincial/District Checklist completion rate’ is calculated by summing up the actual number of times each checklist was filled out by the respective supervisors within the selected date range.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_OVERALL_CHECKLISTS_COMPLETION_RATE_ONE','The Overall Checklists Completion Rate bar chart displays the percentage of supervisors who have completed all the assigned checklists within a selected date range. The chart is divided into three categories: National, Provincial, and District supervisors.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_OVERALL_CHECKLISTS_COMPLETION_RATE_SIX','The bar chart displays the completion rate of checklists for each boundary level (national, provincial, and district), based on the number of checklists assigned and the number of times they were actually completed by the supervisors.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_OVERALL_CHECKLISTS_COMPLETION_RATE_THREE','For National and Provincial Supervisors, the ‘Mandated National/Provincial Checklist completion rate’ is calculated by multiplying the total number of national/provincial supervisors by the sum of the frequency of each checklist for the respective supervisor level. The Mandated District Checklist completion rate is calculated by multiplying the total number of district supervisors by the sum of the frequency of each checklist for the district level.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_OVERALL_CHECKLISTS_COMPLETION_RATE_TWO','The calculation for the completion rate is based on the number of checklists that are mandated for each supervisor level and the actual number of times each checklist was filled out by supervisors within the selected date range.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERAGE_CUMULATIVE','Population coverage (Cumulative)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERAGE_CUMULATIVE_ONE','This metric measures the percentage of the population that has been covered with the intervention (in this case, the distribution of bed nets) against the microplan target. The microplan target refers to the number of individuals that were targeted to receive the intervention according to the project setup.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERAGE_CUMULATIVE_THREE','Additionally, an insight is available to show the percentage change in population coverage from the previous day. This can provide an indication of how quickly the population coverage is increasing or decreasing compared to the previous day.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERAGE_CUMULATIVE_TWO','The calculation takes the sum of the population covered (based on the quantity of bed nets distributed) for the selected province, district, or corresponding district (depending on the user role) since the start of the campaign, and then divides it by the population microplan target for that area. This quotient is then multiplied by 100 to get a percentage.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED','Population Covered',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED_DATE_RANGE','Population covered (For selected date range)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED_DATE_RANGE_FOUR','In other words, we are calculating the total population covered for the selected date range by summing up the population covered for each household within the selected boundary. The boundary data is obtained from MDMS.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED_DATE_RANGE_ONE','In the "Population Covered" metric, firstly, we need to know the population data of the household, which can be found in the "Delivery Intervention" screen and let us denote it as "b".',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED_DATE_RANGE_THREE','For the selected date range, we need to sum up the "a" values for all households within the selected boundary (districts for national and provincial level roles, and Administrative Post for district level roles).',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED_DATE_RANGE_TWO','Then, we calculate the “population covered” for each household by multiplying "b" by 1.8, which is denoted as "a".',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_TARGETED_DATE_RANGE','Population Targeted (For selected date range)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_TARGETED_DATE_RANGE_FOUR','In summary, the "Population Targeted" metric gives an indication of the expected coverage or reach of the campaign, and can help to assess the campaign towards achieving its goals.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_TARGETED_DATE_RANGE_ONE','The "Population Targeted" metric refers to the total number of people that are expected to be reached or covered by the campaign during the selected date range. This metric is based on the microplan targets that were set up during the project setup phase.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_TARGETED_DATE_RANGE_THREE','To calculate the population target for the date range, the microplan targets for the province or district are multiplied by the number of days in the selected date range. This gives an estimate of the total number of people that are expected to be reached or covered during the campaign. The boundary data used for this calculation is obtained from MDMS.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_TARGETED_DATE_RANGE_TWO','The population target varies based on the user role. For the national level role and provincial level role, the population target is for the selected “province”, while for the district level role, it is for the “Administrative Posts”.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_SYNC_RATE','Sync Rate',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_SYNC_RATE_ONE','This indicates the percentage of field workers who have synced their device at least once for the current day, i.e. from 12:00AM to 11:59PM.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE','Total Bed Nets Distributed (Cumulative)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE_FIVE','Overall, this metric provides an indication of the progress of the campaign in distributing bed nets to the targeted population.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE_FOUR','The insight is available for this metric which provides a percent change in the number of bed nets distributed between the current day and the previous day.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE_ONE','This metric represents the total number of bed nets distributed since the start of the campaign, for the selected province, corresponding province, or corresponding district.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE_THREE','This formula is applied for the entire campaign duration, which is calculated as the time between the campaign start date and the current date.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE_TWO','To calculate this metric, the quantity of bed nets distributed to households is captured in the "Delivery Intervention" screen of the application and recorded in the "Quantity distributed" field. The start date of the campaign is determined during the project setup phase, and the boundary data is obtained from the MDMS.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_CUMULATIVE','Total Households Visited (Cumulative)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_CUMULATIVE_ONE','This metric measures the total number of households visited since the start of the campaign. It is calculated by aggregating all the households visited for the selected province or district since the start of the campaign, depending on the user’s role level. The input fields for this metric include the households visited data which is collected by the Field worker application, the campaign start date from the Campaign project setup, and boundary data from MDMS.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_CUMULATIVE_TWO','This also provides additional insights into the percentage change in the number of households visited from the previous day to today.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_CUMULATIVE','Total Population Covered (Cumulative)',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_CUMULATIVE_FOUR','Overall, the Total Population Covered (Cumulative) metric provides an indication of how effective the intervention has been in reaching the target population and meeting the campaign goals.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_CUMULATIVE_ONE','The Total Population Covered (Cumulative) is a metric that shows the total population covered since the start of the campaign, and it is used for monitoring the progress of the intervention in reaching the target population. This metric is applicable for all user roles: national, provincial, and district level, the data will be displayed as per the boundaries permission allotted.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_CUMULATIVE_THREE','Additionally, an insight is available for this metric, which is (Today - Previous day) / Previous Day * 100. This insight shows the percentage increase or decrease in the metric from the previous day to the current day.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_CUMULATIVE_TWO','To calculate this metric, we use the Population Data for household Covered, which is obtained by multiplying the Quantity of bednets Distributed to the household by 1.8. The campaign start date is obtained from the Project Setup, and the Boundary data is obtained from the MDMS.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_USERS_CREATED','Total Users Created',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_USERS_CREATED_ONE','The "Total users created" KPI card refers to the total number of field workers who have been created in the user management module. This includes all field workers who have been assigned to the campaign in a particular province. The total number of staff created and assigned to the campaign is determined by the boundary, which can be at the province or district level. The Dashboard displays the user-created data, based on the user type of the dashboard.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_USERS_SYNCED_ATLEAST_ONCE','Total Users Synced At Least Once',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_USERS_SYNCED_ATLEAST_ONCE_ONE','This key performance indicator (KPI) measures the number of field workers who have synchronized their data at least once in a day using the "sync tag" button on their mobile application. The count includes unique syncs from different field workers, and multiple syncs from the same device will only be counted as one. The time frame for a day is from 12:00AM to 11:59PM.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_USERS_SYNCED_ATLEAST_ONCE_TWO',' It''s important to note that if a field worker has synced their data once but after that it has unsynced data, it will not be reflected in this KPI.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REEGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TAB_OVERVIEW_ONE','The "Registration and Delivery" section in the dashboard provides information about the field workers who are involved in two different activities: household registration and intervention delivery.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REEGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TAB_OVERVIEW_TWO','The data displayed to the user is totally as per the user role who is viewing:',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED','Bed Nets Distributed',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_FOUR','Overall, this metric provides insight into the effectiveness of bed net distribution efforts within a given area and time period.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_ONE','The Bed nets Distributed KPI shows a bar chart with the total number of bed nets distributed within a selected date range and boundary. The data is collected from the Delivery Intervention Screen in the mobile application, specifically the Quantity distributed field.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_THREE','For the “%” toggle, the metric is calculated as the percentage of bed nets distributed compared to the daily Bed nets Micro plan target for each district or administrative province, multiplied by the number of days in the selected date range.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_TWO','For the “Number” toggle, the metric is calculated as the sum of bed nets distributed for each household within the selected date range and boundary.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_NOT_DELIVERED','Bed Nets Not Delivered',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_NOT_DELIVERED_ONE','The KPI for "Bed Nets Not Delivered" is a measure of the number of households where bed net delivery did not take place within a selected date range.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_NOT_DELIVERED_THREE','The data displayed in the bar chart in the number count for this metric, which displays the total number of households with no bed net delivery for the selected date range, broken down by district or administrative post region, depending on the user''s role.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_NOT_DELIVERED_TWO','To calculate this metric, the data is taken from the application, specifically the count of resources delivered for each household. The total number of households with no bed net delivery is then aggregated and displayed as a bar chart.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED','Households Visited',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_FIVE','For example, for national and provincial roles, the chart will show the percentage of households visited in each district compared to the daily households microplan target. For district roles, the chart will show the percentage of households visited in each administrative province compared to the daily households microplan target.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_FOUR','In the "%", toggle the chart shows the percentage of households visited for the selected date range in each district or administrative province, compared to the daily households microplan target and the number of days in the date range selection. ',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_MAP','Households Visited',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_MAP_ONE','The "Households visited" section in the dashboard provides a map with latitude/longitude coordinates of the households that have been visited within the selected boundary. The map can be zoomed in or out for better clarity of the households.',1,now(),1,now()),
