(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_FAQ_ACRYNOMS_LISTED_BELOW','The Acronyms that are used in DSS and their full forms are listed below',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_FAQ_ADMINISTRATIVE_POST','Administrative Post',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_FAQ_ANS_CAMPAIGN_LEVEL_USER_VIEW','Different user roles have access to different levels of campaign data:',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_FAQ_ANS_DEFINITION_OF_KPI','To find the definitions of various KPIs, you can hover your mouse pointer over each KPI, and the definition will appear.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_FAQ_ANS_LIST_OF_PROVINCES','The list of provinces where a selected campaign is running can only be viewed by a user with the National Level User role. Once they log in and select the campaign from the list, they will be directed to the national dashboard. To find the list of provinces, the user can scroll to the bottom of the page where they will see a card with the title "Coverage by Province". This card contains a list of all the provinces where the selected campaign is being implemented.',1,now(),1,now()),
(gen_random_uuid()::text,'mz','en_MZ','rainmaker-hcm-dss','DSS_FAQ_ANS_NATIONAL_USER_VIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS','To view the total count of Bednets distributed across a healthcare campaign, a national-level user can follow these steps:',1,now(),1,now()),
